1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,370
In the middle of the ocean...

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:04,049
above the waves...

3
00:00:04,419 --> 00:00:06,669
a fighter jet is coming in

4
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:06,969
fast.

5
00:00:07,740 --> 00:00:10,759
Around two hundred and fifty kilometres

6
00:00:10,710 --> 00:00:11,359
an hour.

7
00:00:11,929 --> 00:00:12,890
Ahead of it,

8
00:00:12,980 --> 00:00:15,089
a runway just a few hundred

9
00:00:15,039 --> 00:00:15,839
metres long...

10
00:00:16,210 --> 00:00:18,199
on a ship that is moving.

11
00:00:19,070 --> 00:00:19,929
And then...

12
00:00:20,300 --> 00:00:21,940
in about three seconds...

13
00:00:22,309 --> 00:00:24,489
the jet comes to a complete

14
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:24,750
stop.

15
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,250
This is INS Vikrant.

16
00:00:28,820 --> 00:00:30,690
Designed in India,

17
00:00:30,780 --> 00:00:32,299
built in India.

18
00:00:32,570 --> 00:00:34,979
India's own aircraft carrier.

19
00:00:35,850 --> 00:00:38,219
More than two hundred and sixty

20
00:00:38,170 --> 00:00:38,990
metres long,

21
00:00:39,079 --> 00:00:41,320
this ship is an entire city

22
00:00:41,270 --> 00:00:42,600
floating on the sea.

23
00:00:43,270 --> 00:00:45,170
But how do jets take off

24
00:00:45,119 --> 00:00:46,750
from such a short runway?

25
00:00:47,020 --> 00:00:48,590
And how do they land?

26
00:00:49,460 --> 00:00:51,549
Let's step inside Vikrant.

27
00:00:53,219 --> 00:00:54,880
A name that came back.

28
00:00:55,950 --> 00:00:58,179
Vikrant is not a new name.

29
00:00:58,750 --> 00:01:01,490
India's very first aircraft carrier was

30
00:01:01,439 --> 00:01:03,049
also called Vikrant,

31
00:01:03,289 --> 00:01:04,890
and it played a key role

32
00:01:04,840 --> 00:01:07,219
in the war of nineteen seventy-one.

33
00:01:08,090 --> 00:01:09,819
After years of service,

34
00:01:09,909 --> 00:01:12,340
that old Vikrant was retired.

35
00:01:13,310 --> 00:01:15,120
In twenty twenty-two,

36
00:01:15,209 --> 00:01:16,829
the name returned...

37
00:01:17,200 --> 00:01:18,430
but this time,

38
00:01:18,519 --> 00:01:20,519
on a new and far bigger

39
00:01:20,469 --> 00:01:20,810
ship,

40
00:01:20,900 --> 00:01:23,180
built entirely in India.

41
00:01:23,950 --> 00:01:26,340
It was built at Cochin Shipyard,

42
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:29,189
and designed by the Indian Navy's

43
00:01:29,140 --> 00:01:30,230
own engineers.

44
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:31,819
With it,

45
00:01:31,909 --> 00:01:34,260
India joined a small group of

46
00:01:34,209 --> 00:01:36,569
nations that can design and build

47
00:01:36,519 --> 00:01:38,239
their own aircraft carrier.

48
00:01:39,909 --> 00:01:41,719
A city on the sea.

49
00:01:42,790 --> 00:01:43,549
Now,

50
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,189
think about its size.

51
00:01:45,859 --> 00:01:47,709
It is about as long as

52
00:01:47,659 --> 00:01:48,700
two football fields.

53
00:01:49,269 --> 00:01:52,280
It weighs around forty-five thousand tonnes.

54
00:01:53,049 --> 00:01:54,040
Inside,

55
00:01:54,129 --> 00:01:56,439
there are more than two thousand

56
00:01:56,390 --> 00:01:57,560
rooms and compartments.

57
00:01:57,829 --> 00:01:58,840
Many decks,

58
00:01:58,930 --> 00:02:00,329
long corridors,

59
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:02,439
and a maze of ladders.

60
00:02:03,209 --> 00:02:06,230
Around sixteen hundred people live here.

61
00:02:06,799 --> 00:02:09,240
A huge galley cooks for thousands,

62
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:10,629
day and night.

63
00:02:11,400 --> 00:02:13,759
There is even a full hospital

64
00:02:13,710 --> 00:02:14,289
on board,

65
00:02:14,379 --> 00:02:17,099
with an operating theatre and an

66
00:02:17,050 --> 00:02:17,610
ICU.

67
00:02:18,379 --> 00:02:21,780
And its engines generate enough electricity

68
00:02:21,729 --> 00:02:23,370
to light up a small town.

69
00:02:24,139 --> 00:02:26,400
Its power comes from four large

70
00:02:26,349 --> 00:02:27,319
gas turbines,

71
00:02:27,409 --> 00:02:29,349
which can push this giant ship

72
00:02:29,300 --> 00:02:32,280
faster than thirty kilometres an hour.

73
00:02:33,050 --> 00:02:35,810
Even its special steel was developed

74
00:02:35,759 --> 00:02:36,590
in India.

75
00:02:38,259 --> 00:02:40,229
Take-off from a ski-jump.

76
00:02:41,300 --> 00:02:42,069
Now,

77
00:02:42,159 --> 00:02:44,050
the most interesting part.

78
00:02:44,319 --> 00:02:45,319
On land,

79
00:02:45,409 --> 00:02:47,710
a fighter jet usually needs a

80
00:02:47,659 --> 00:02:49,500
long runway to take off.

81
00:02:50,169 --> 00:02:51,969
But a ship doesn't have that

82
00:02:51,919 --> 00:02:52,669
much space.

83
00:02:53,439 --> 00:02:55,050
So at Vikrant's bow,

84
00:02:55,139 --> 00:02:57,030
the runway curves upward,

85
00:02:57,120 --> 00:02:58,580
like a ski slope.

86
00:02:58,849 --> 00:03:00,979
This is called a ski-jump.

87
00:03:01,849 --> 00:03:03,259
Before take-off,

88
00:03:03,349 --> 00:03:05,340
the jet is held in place

89
00:03:05,289 --> 00:03:06,210
on the deck,

90
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:08,300
while its engine spools up to

91
00:03:08,250 --> 00:03:08,960
full power.

92
00:03:09,830 --> 00:03:11,460
Then it is released...

93
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:13,659
it races down the deck...

94
00:03:14,030 --> 00:03:16,169
and the ski-jump throws it upward

95
00:03:16,120 --> 00:03:17,219
into the air.

96
00:03:17,990 --> 00:03:20,219
That upward throw gives the jet

97
00:03:20,169 --> 00:03:22,110
the vital moment it needs,

98
00:03:22,199 --> 00:03:24,159
for its wings to grip the

99
00:03:24,110 --> 00:03:25,759
air and reach flying speed.

100
00:03:27,430 --> 00:03:29,379
The three-second miracle.

101
00:03:30,449 --> 00:03:32,259
Taking off is hard...

102
00:03:32,629 --> 00:03:34,849
but landing is even harder.

103
00:03:35,620 --> 00:03:37,490
Under the tail of the jet

104
00:03:37,439 --> 00:03:38,580
is a strong hook,

105
00:03:38,669 --> 00:03:40,050
called a tailhook.

106
00:03:40,819 --> 00:03:43,090
Across the deck lie thick steel

107
00:03:43,039 --> 00:03:43,650
cables,

108
00:03:43,740 --> 00:03:45,599
called arrestor wires.

109
00:03:46,370 --> 00:03:48,129
The pilot has to land so

110
00:03:48,080 --> 00:03:50,000
that the hook catches one of

111
00:03:49,949 --> 00:03:50,860
these wires.

112
00:03:51,629 --> 00:03:53,419
The hook snags the wire...

113
00:03:53,789 --> 00:03:55,319
the wire pulls out...

114
00:03:55,689 --> 00:03:58,250
and machines below the deck absorb

115
00:03:58,199 --> 00:03:58,830
that pull,

116
00:03:58,919 --> 00:04:00,340
little by little.

117
00:04:01,210 --> 00:04:03,229
And a jet arriving at two

118
00:04:03,180 --> 00:04:05,729
hundred and fifty kilometres an hour

119
00:04:05,680 --> 00:04:07,699
comes to a stop in about

120
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:08,419
three seconds.

121
00:04:09,490 --> 00:04:11,560
And if the hook misses every

122
00:04:11,509 --> 00:04:11,979
wire?

123
00:04:12,250 --> 00:04:14,979
The pilot instantly pushes the engine

124
00:04:14,930 --> 00:04:16,240
back to full power,

125
00:04:16,329 --> 00:04:18,329
and the jet takes off again,

126
00:04:18,420 --> 00:04:19,759
for another try.

127
00:04:21,430 --> 00:04:23,300
Guardian of the seas.

128
00:04:24,370 --> 00:04:27,370
Vikrant can carry around thirty aircraft,

129
00:04:27,459 --> 00:04:30,339
fighter jets and helicopters together.

130
00:04:31,110 --> 00:04:33,000
Wherever this ship goes,

131
00:04:33,089 --> 00:04:35,259
it takes an entire airbase with

132
00:04:35,209 --> 00:04:35,490
it.

133
00:04:36,259 --> 00:04:38,279
Eyes far across the ocean,

134
00:04:38,370 --> 00:04:41,040
and an instant answer when needed.

135
00:04:42,509 --> 00:04:44,050
So the next time you look

136
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:45,689
at a picture of the sea...

137
00:04:46,060 --> 00:04:46,970
remember.

138
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:49,750
Somewhere among those waves,

139
00:04:49,839 --> 00:04:52,379
a floating city built in India

140
00:04:52,329 --> 00:04:54,350
stands guard over the nation.

141
00:04:55,519 --> 00:04:57,389
INS Vikrant...

142
00:04:57,759 --> 00:04:59,509
India on the sea.

143
00:05:00,779 --> 00:05:03,209
What surprised you the most about

144
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:03,709
Vikrant?

145
00:05:03,980 --> 00:05:05,620
Tell us in the comments.

